  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000123046,
      "SummaryText": "Better Baked Foods, LLC, current Emergency Response Plan focuses on evacuation and response of the facility in the event of an ammonia emergency.  Better Baked Foods, LLC, works closely with the Local Emergency Planning Committee and Erie County Emergency Management and HazMat team on emergency preparedness.  The written plan is promptly updated to reflect any pertinent changes taking place within the facility that would require modified procedures.\n\n- Planned Changes to Improve Safety:\n\nBetter Baked Foods, LLC, currently has no changes planned for the ammonia refrigeration processes at this time.   However, the processes will be subjected to periodic process hazard analysis reviews for the purpose of identifying potential hazards and implementing the necessary improvement to provide a safer system. Better Baked Foods, LLC, personnel will also periodically review all potential opportunities to improve the safety of our personnel, the surrounding community, and the ammonia refrigeration processes."
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123046,
      "SummaryText": "EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n- Accidental Release Prevention and Emergency Response Policies\n\nBetter Baked Foods, LLC (SFC Global Supply Chain) North East, PA, is strongly committed to employee, public, and environmental safety. This commitment is inherent to our comprehensive accidental release prevention program that covers areas such as design, installation, operating procedures, maintenance, and employee training associated with our regulated process. It is our policy to implement appropriate controls to prevent possible accidental releases of regulated substances. However, if such an accidental release does occur, we are coordinated with the Erie County Emergency Management and the Erie County Local Emergency Planning Committee for emergency response support.\n\n\n- The Stationary Source and the Regulated Substances Handled\n\nPresently Anhydrous Ammonia is the only RMP regulated substance present at this facility above a threshold quantity.  Ammonia is utilized as the primary cooling media in our closed-loop refrigeration system. The system's purpose is to provide refrigeration and cold storage capabilities for Better Baked Foods, LLC, operations.  Due to the size and characteristics of our ammonia refrigeration systems, as well as Process Safety Management (PSM) applicability, Better Baked Foods, LLC, is covered under Program 3 of the RMP regulations.\n\n- General Accidental Release Prevention Program \n\nBetter Baked Foods, LLC, has taken all necessary steps to comply with the accidental release prevention requirements set forth in 40 CFR Part 68.  To meet these necessary requirements Better Baked Foods, LLC, has implemented their Process Safety Management program through the written guidelines stated in the OSHA PSM Standard, 29 CFR 1910.119. \n\n- Accident History\n\nIn the past five years, Better Baked Foods, LLC, has not experienced any accidental releases of ammonia that resulted in on site or off site impacts, or that required reporting.  \n\n- Emergency Action/Response Plan"
    }
  ]
